# Game assets (owner: `artist`)

Everything the game loads is listed in `manifest.json` (shape and names: `world/game-developer` `docs/assets.md`).

- `sprites/player.png` — Mario: `small_*`, `big_*`, `fire_*`, `star1_*`..`star3_*` (facing right, bottom-centre anchored).
- `sprites/enemies_<theme>.png` — enemies (facing left); base = overworld, variants underground / castle.
- `sprites/items_<theme>.png` — items, effects, score popups, HUD coin, menu cursor, flags, axe, bridge, chain.
- `tiles/<theme>.png`, `tiles/scenery_<theme>.png` — level tiles and background pictures.
- `ui/font.png` (8×8 grid, `font.chars`), `ui/title.png` (title board).
- `audio/sfx/*`, `audio/music/*` — chiptune SFX, music loops (`loopStart`/`loopEnd` in seconds) and jingles.

All graphics and audio are original work made for this project in the NES 8-bit style
(no ROM data, no ripped sprites, no recorded or transcribed Nintendo music).
They are generated from source in `tools/` of `world/artist`:

    python3 tools/gfx/build_gfx.py        # sprites, tiles, font, title  -> assets/, build/gfx.json
    python3 tools/audio/build_audio.py    # SFX + music                  -> assets/audio/
    python3 tools/build_manifest.py       # merge + validate             -> assets/manifest.json

`tools/build_manifest.py` fails on a missing file, a rect outside its image or a stray file,
and lists every name from the game's contract (`tools/required_names.txt`) still missing.
